From: serenitea-pot <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] aipu: reject unsupported IOMMU domains

The Zhouyi v3 allocator programs explicit IOVAs, so identity domains created
by iommu.passthrough cannot support it. Its fallback path also dereferences the
DMA-IOMMU cookie while reserving forbidden IOVA ranges. Reject a missing or
identity domain cleanly instead of failing mappings or dereferencing NULL.

---
diff --git a/armchina-npu/aipu_mm.c b/armchina-npu/aipu_mm.c
--- a/armchina-npu/aipu_mm.c
+++ b/armchina-npu/aipu_mm.c
@@ -1735,6 +1735,17 @@ int aipu_init_mm(struct aipu_memory_manager *mm, struct platform_device *p_dev,
 	if (group) {
 		mm->has_iommu = true;
 		mm->iommu_domain = iommu_get_domain_for_dev(mm->dev);
+		if (!mm->iommu_domain ||
+		    (mm->version == AIPU_ISA_VERSION_ZHOUYI_V3 &&
+		     !mm->iommu_domain->iova_cookie)) {
+			dev_err(mm->dev,
+				"Zhouyi v3 requires an IOMMU DMA domain; disable iommu.passthrough\n");
+			mm->has_iommu = false;
+			ret = -ENODEV;
+			iommu_group_put(group);
+			goto finish;
+		}
+
 		if (mm->version >= AIPU_ISA_VERSION_ZHOUYI_V3_2) {
 			mm->valid_asid_cnt = 0;
 			mm->iova_base = 0x100000000ULL;   // start from 4GB
